.TH SDL_Vulkan_GetInstanceExtensions 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_Vulkan_GetInstanceExtensions \- Get the Vulkan instance extensions needed for vkCreateInstance.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_vulkan.h>
.PP
.BI "char const * const * SDL_Vulkan_GetInstanceExtensions(Uint32 *count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This should be called after either calling
.BR SDL_Vulkan_LoadLibrary ()
or creating an
.BR SDL_Window
with the
.BR SDL_WINDOW_VULKAN
flag\[char46]
.PP
On return, the variable pointed to by
.BR count
will be set to the number of elements returned, suitable for using with VkInstanceCreateInfo::enabledExtensionCount, and the returned array can be used with VkInstanceCreateInfo::ppEnabledExtensionNames, for calling Vulkan\(aqs vkCreateInstance API\[char46]
.PP
You should not free the returned array; it is owned by SDL\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I count
a pointer filled in with the number of extensions returned\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an array of extension name strings on success, NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_Vulkan_CreateSurface (3)
